  "notes": "General Biology option, University Park, standard MATH 140 start (the bulletin also has an ALEKS/MATH-21-remedial-start variant and a MATH-22/26-start variant). Uses the CHEM 210/212/213W organic-chemistry path rather than the CHEM 202/203 alternative, matching the University Park suggested plan. The '18 credits of 400-level biology, with at least 3 from each of 6 named groups (Plant and Fungi, Evolution, Genetics and Developmental Biology, Ecology, Physiology, Practicum)' requirement is modeled as 6 slots of 3 credits each (one per group) \u2014 the bulletin's own suggested plan does the same thing, listing these generically as 'BIOL 4XX' rather than specific codes, since each group has 20-30 alternative courses. 'Supporting Courses and Related Areas' (24-31 credits department-list electives) and remaining Gen Ed requirements are modeled as generic slots. 'etm' marks the courses everything else in the sequence assumes are done. For 2022-23/2023-24, MATH 141 was an additional common-major prescribed course (added here in Semester 3, replacing one Supporting Course slot to stay within the credit cap) and the organic-chem lab used plain CHEM 213 (not the 213/213W/213M alternative).",
